-- title:
--   A height-one prime of the j-integral closure as a place over K
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (the algebraic closure of $\mathbb Q$ as constructed in Mathlib), a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ and a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red}\colon A \to k$, and let $K$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$ that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb Q$. Write $F =$ `fieldOver (1 * q) K` for the subfield of the Laurent series field $\overline{\mathbb Q}((X))$ generated by the constant series attached to elements of $K$ together with the two series `jqModC` and `jqNModC` of level $1\cdot q$, write $R =$ `jRing A K` for the subring generated by the constant series of elements of $A \cap K$ together with `jqModC`, and let $C =$ `jIntegralClosure (1 * q) A K` be the subring of elements of $F$ that are integral over $R$. Let $\mathfrak p \subset C$ be a prime ideal of height $1$ such that, for every nonzero $b \in A \cap K$ whose constant series lies in $C$, that constant series is not in $\mathfrak p$. The conclusion asserts the existence of a place $V$ of $F$ over $K$ in the sense of the project structure `Place`, i.e. a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$ itself and a principal ideal ring, whose elements are exactly those $g \in F$ for which $g s = r$ for some $r, s \in C$ with $s \notin \mathfrak p$; that is, the valuation ring of $V$ is the localisation $C_{\mathfrak p}$.
--
--   This is the passage from a horizontal height-one prime of the normalised model to a point of the curve, packaged as a place of the function field $F$ over $K$ with valuation ring $C_{\mathfrak p}$. It is used in [`ModularCurve.exists_place_centred_node_of_height_one_of_natCast_notMem`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_place_centred_node_of_height_one_of_natCast_notMem), in the construction of places centred at the nodes of the modular curve.
